<% @page_title = "Plugins" %>
<%= render "settings/header", current: :plugins %>

<section class="settings settings--wide">
  <div class="settings__panel panel shadow txt-align-start">
    <section class="settings__section flex flex-column gap">
      <header>
        <h2 class="divider">Installed plugins</h2>
      </header>
      <p class="txt-small txt-subtle margin-none">Plugins add to the core without changing it. Bundled plugins come with Runwell <%= Runwell::VERSION %>; others are installed from a git repository (below). Every plugin starts off: switch it on here. Switching one off hides everything it adds and keeps its data.</p>

      <ul class="plugin-cards">
        <% @plugins.each do |plugin| %>
          <%# herb:key plugin.key %>
          <%= render "settings/plugins/plugin", plugin: plugin, enabled: Runwell::Plugins.enabled?(plugin.key) %>
        <% end %>
      </ul>

      <% if @plugins.none? %>
        <div class="blank-slate">No plugins installed.</div>
      <% end %>
    </section>

    <section class="settings__section flex flex-column gap">
      <header>
        <h2 class="divider">Add a plugin</h2>
      </header>
      <p class="txt-small txt-subtle margin-none">A plugin is a git repository (on GitHub or anywhere). On the server, from Runwell’s directory:</p>
      <pre class="txt-small margin-none"><code>bin/rails "plugins:install[https://github.com/org/runwell-thing]"</code></pre>
      <p class="txt-small txt-subtle margin-none">That clones it into <code>plugins/</code>, bundles, migrates and restarts; then it appears here, off. <code>plugins:update[name]</code> pulls a newer version and <code>plugins:remove[name]</code> takes it out. A Docker install rebuilds its image afterwards.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>
